@Graur I have an idea how to implement it in EO. As I understand `string.as-bytes` gives byte representation of string in encoding UTF-8. So, for example, the word `HELLO` look like `48 45 4c 4c 4f`. We can convert it to `hello` according to the ASCII table by adding `20` to each byte of `HELLO`: `68 65 6c 6c 6f`  <-  this is `hello`. 

First, I want to hear your opinion about this. Perhaps some other implementation is implied. 
Second, if this idea is good, how can we add bytes in EO in this way. If there aren't any methods for this mb I can create?
